{"term":"engineer","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ccaf289665ca69e682","definition":"A soldier engaged in designing or constructing military works for attack or defence, or other engineering works.","example":"For tis the ſport to haue the enginer / Hoiſt with his ovvne petar, an't ſhall goe hard / But I vvill delue one yard belovve their mines, / And blovve them at the Moone: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, figuratively","wordFamily":["astroengineer","bioneer","engineer boot","engineeress","engineerish","engineerization","engineer's blue","engineer's chain","engineership","engineer's scale","enginerd","engr.","fungineer","glycoengineer","Imagineer","microengineer","misengineer","motorneer","nanoengineer","neuroengineer","nonengineer","nonengineering","socioengineer","subengineer","tractioneer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engineer#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:831018ed364d09f962","definition":"A soldier in charge of operating a weapon; an artilleryman, a gunner.","example":"This is hard welcome, but it was not you, / At whom the fatal enginer did ayme, / My breaſt the levell was, though you the marke, / In which conſpiracie anſwere me Duke, / Is not thy ſoule as guiltie as the Earles?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively, obsolete","register":"also, figuratively, obsolete","wordFamily":["astroengineer","bioneer","engineer boot","engineeress","engineerish","engineerization","engineer's blue","engineer's chain","engineership","engineer's scale","enginerd","engr.","fungineer","glycoengineer","Imagineer","microengineer","misengineer","motorneer","nanoengineer","neuroengineer","nonengineer","nonengineering","socioengineer","subengineer","tractioneer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engineer#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25eadbc24b25bb91de","definition":"A person professionally engaged in the technical design and construction of large-scale private and public works such as bridges, buildings, harbours, railways, roads, etc.; a civil engineer.","example":"[T]o an Enginer alſo, vvho promiſed to bring into the Capitoll huge Columnes vvith ſmall charges, hee gave for his deviſe no meane revvard; and releaſed him his labour in performing that vvorke, ſaying vvithall by vvay of preface, That he ſhould ſuffer him to feed the poore commons.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["hostler"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["astroengineer","bioneer","engineer boot","engineeress","engineerish","engineerization","engineer's blue","engineer's chain","engineership","engineer's scale","enginerd","engr.","fungineer","glycoengineer","Imagineer","microengineer","misengineer","motorneer","nanoengineer","neuroengineer","nonengineer","nonengineering","socioengineer","subengineer","tractioneer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/engineer#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d898c6ddf65545d2a9","definition":"Originally, a person engaged in designing, constructing, or maintaining engines or machinery; now (more generally), a person qualified or professionally engaged in any branch of engineering, or studying to do so.","example":"Macanopoietico, an inginer, an engine-maker.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["hostler"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["astroengineer","bioneer","engineer boot","engineeress","engineerish","engineerization","engineer's blue","engineer's chain","engineership","engineer's scale","enginerd","engr.","fungineer","glycoengineer","Imagineer","microengineer","misengineer"